 "meta": {
  "standard": "ISO 286-1 / ISO 286-2 (ISO system of limits and fits), tabulated values for nominal sizes up to 500 mm",
  "edition_note": "Values follow the 2010 editions; ISO 286-1:2010 supersedes ISO 286-1:1988.",
  "deviation_unit": "micrometre",
  "size_unit": "mm",
  "transcription": "Transcribed by hand from the published ISO 286-1 tables; not copied from any software package or data file. Cross-checked in tests against the isofits package (MIT, test-only) and the ISO 286-1 formulas. The standard itself is authoritative.",
  "size_range_rule": "ranges are lower-exclusive and upper-inclusive: a size of 18 mm belongs to 10-18; 3 mm belongs to 0-3",
  "hole_rules": "A..H and CD, EF, FG: EI = -es of the shaft position with the same letter. JS: +/-IT/2 exactly. J: tabulated ES (IT6 to IT8). K, M, N up to IT8 and P..ZC up to IT7: ES = -ei + delta with delta = IT(n) - IT(n-1) of the same size range, and 0 for sizes up to 3 mm; K uses the tabulated k value for IT8 too. Above those grades: ES = -ei (K: 0; N above IT8 and over 3 mm: 0).",
  "shaft_rules": "a..g: es tabulated, ei = es - IT. h: es = 0. js: +/-IT/2. j: ei tabulated for IT5 to IT7. k: ei tabulated for IT4 to IT7, 0 otherwise. m..zc: ei tabulated, es = ei + IT. null = position not defined for that size range.",
  "verification": "Every shaft position (a..zc) and every hole rule was compared cell for cell with an independent published fundamental-deviation table (RoyMech, 0 to 500 mm) and, for 3 to 400 mm, with the isofits package; remaining disagreements are source typos resolved by the standard's own rules (see docs/iso286-data.md). zb 280-315 mm is 1300 (two independent tables and the ISO formula agree), not 1350."
 },
